\subtree{
  \title{Decision}
  \p{Every universal object is \em{a} witness of a Prop-valued universal property. No global choice functions (\code{limit F}, \code{X ⨯ Y}) exist. \code{lift}-style operations are \code{Classical.choose} on unique existence or contractibility. Theorems quantify over witnesses. Witnesses of a given universal property form a contractible space (1-level: a contractible groupoid), and transport between witnesses is functoriality in the witness.}
}
\subtree{
  \title{Rationale}
  \p{Definitional uniqueness is a lie about mathematics; contractibility of the witness space is the truth, and it is the statement that survives the passage to ∞.}
}
\subtree{
  \title{Rejected}
  \p{Data-valued universal properties with \code{Subsingleton} instances (keeps a constructive door open, but reintroduces the temptation to unfold \code{lift}). Chosen-limit typeclasses (instance diamonds).}
}
\subtree{
  \title{Status}
  \p{frozen.}
}
